; Print a character in the current output window
;
; The one character output of the game. Does nothing when #R$8576 says output
; is off. Otherwise sends the character to the input window (#R$85B7) when
; RawOutputFlag is set, or to the story window (#R$86A1). In the story window,
; while LispFlag is set, an S or s is followed by an H, so that the speaker
; lisps (the extra H goes through the same story window routine, with its
; capital and line end rules).
; .
; Hardware: none itself; the windows draw on the screen.
;
; A Character code ($0D new line, $08 back-space, $20-$7F printable)
; O:F Z set when output is off (nothing printed)
@label=PrintChar
c$858B CALL $8576    ; output enabled?
 $858E RET Z         ;
 $858F PUSH AF       ;
 $8590 LD A,($B701)  ;
 $8593 AND A         ;
 $8594 JR NZ,$85B7   ; RawOutputFlag set: the input window
 $8596 POP AF        ;
 $8597 CALL $86A1    ; story window
 $859A PUSH AF       ;
 $859B LD A,($B700)  ;
 $859E AND A         ;
 $859F JR NZ,$85A3   ; LispFlag set
 $85A1 POP AF        ;
 $85A2 RET           ;
*$85A3 POP AF        ;
@isub=CP 'S'
 $85A4 CP $53        ;
 $85A6 JR Z,$85AB    ;
@isub=CP 's'
 $85A8 CP $73        ;
 $85AA RET NZ        ;
*$85AB PUSH AF       ;
@isub=LD A,'H'
 $85AC LD A,$48      ;
 $85AE CALL $86A1    ; S -> SH
 $85B1 POP AF        ;
 $85B2 RET           ;
